# Installed to $HOME/.gitignore by bin/cfg-install. Deliberately NOT tracked as
# a plain .gitignore: the cfg repo's work tree is $HOME in a deployment, but is
# an ordinary directory in a development clone (e.g. ~/projects/cfg), and a
# deny-all committed at the repo root would make every `git add` there need -f
# too. The deny-all is a property of the deployment, so the installer copies it
# into place and re-syncs it on each run.
#
# Deny everything by default. Without this, a single `cfg add -A` stages the
# whole home directory -- ssh keys, Documents, .cfg itself -- and this repo is
# public. Note that `status.showUntrackedFiles=no` does NOT protect against
# that: it only hides untracked files from `cfg status`, so the working tree
# looks clean right up until you stage a private key.
#
# Ignoring `*` does not affect files that are ALREADY tracked -- they stay
# tracked and their modifications still show up in `cfg status`. It only stops
# new files being picked up automatically.
#
# So: to add a new dotfile you must force it, deliberately, one at a time:
#
#     cfg add -f .some-new-rc
#
# N.B. this file only applies to the cfg repo. Other repos (e.g. under
# ~/projects) have their own roots below $HOME and never read it.

*

# --- Belt and braces ------------------------------------------------------
# `*` above already covers these. They are spelled out so that the protection
# survives anyone later relaxing the deny-all, and to document what must never
# be committed. `cfg add -f` would override `*`, but not these.

# Private keys and credentials. Only the ssh *config* files are tracked here
# (.ssh/remote_config, .ssh/remote_jasmin_config, and the gpg-encrypted
# ssh_config_zerogravitas.gpg) -- never key material.
.ssh/id_*
!.ssh/id_*.pub
.ssh/known_hosts*
.ssh/authorized_keys
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.netrc
.pgpass

# Cloud / API credentials that like to live in $HOME.
.aws/
.config/gcloud/
.kube/
.docker/config.json
.npmrc
.pypirc
.git-credentials

# MOSRS / Rose / conda state, none of which belongs in version control.
.rose*/
.cylc/
.metomi/
.conda/
.condarc.local

# The repo's own git dir and the installer's backups.
.cfg/
.cfg-backup/

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
._*
.Trash/
